Painless Install

# 1. Create the database
sqlite3 file_archive.db < schema.sql

# 2. Populate from existing Markdown (if any)
./migrate_md_to_sqlite.sh file_archive.db files_index.md

# 3. Start ingesting new files (SQLite will be populated)
./file_ingest.sh add ~/Videos "movies" false "videos" "movies"

# 4. Launch the web UI
python3 app.py

# 5. Open http://localhost:8080 and explore!



WEB APP USING
pip install flask

# 2. Place app.py and the templates/ folder in your project directory

# 3. Make sure your SQLite database exists (file_archive.db) and has the schema

# 4. Set the DB path (optional)
export DB_PATH=./file_archive.db

# 5. Start the web server
python3 app.py

# 6. Open your browser to http://localhost:8080
